  "fullDescription": "Procreate Christmas Tree Brushes, Christmas Tree Brushes, Christmas Tree Brush, Christmas Brushes, Christmas Brush, Christmas procreate, Tree Brushes, Tree Brush, Trees Brushes, Trees Brush, Tree procreate, Christmas Tree, procreate, Procreate brushes stamp, procreate brush stamp, procreate brushes, procreate brush, brushes stamp, brush stamp, procreate, addons procreate\n\nProcreate Christmas Tree Brushes. There are 50 individual stamps included in this procreate brush. These stamp brushes are great for creating digital and printable projects which are graphic design, stationery & printable, doodles, Instagram posts, blog posts, wall art, surface patterns, packaging, posters, business cards, illustrations, blog buttons, etc.\n\nYOU WILL RECEIVE:\n– 1 Zip of brush set file with 50 stamps created in Procreate.\n\nHOW TO USE:\n– Download the brush set file and import it to your brushes in Procreate\n(Use with Procreate only!).\n– After install, choose a stamp and tap on your screen for your design.\n– You can scale / resize these stamp brushes, change opacity, color or set-ups.\n\nHOW TO INSTALL?\n– Open IPAD\n– Unzip file\n– Download brush set file and it will automatically import into procreate brush collection.\n\nIF NOT, DO THIS TUTORIAL:\n1. Download brush set file to folder on your iPad\n2. Open the folder and find downloaded brush set file\n3. Tap and hold with your finger or apple pencil\n4. Choose “Share” from the menu\n5. If the option “Open in Procreate” is missing, click on “More”\n6. Scroll and find the option “Open in Procreate” and click on it\n7. Open your project in Procreate and click on brush icon at the top right corner\n8. Find the new brush set in your Brush library\n\nIMPORTANT:\n– Use these brushes with Procreate App on IPAD only\n– These brushes DO NOT work in Photoshop or any other application.\n– This is a digital product. No physical product will be sent to you.\n\nBest Regard,\nTanvara T/.",
